    "这台解析器不给递归查询（常见于只服务内网的 DNS），换一台公共 DNS 再问。": "This resolver won't do recursive queries (common on DNS that only serves the intranet); try a public DNS.",
    "这台解析器只服务内网（不替你查公网名字）。换一台公共 DNS，": "This resolver only serves the intranet (it won't look up public names for you). Switch to a public DNS,",
    "这台认这个应用，但「这路在不在推」没问": "This device knows this app, but \"is this stream being published\" was not asked",
    "这台设备认这个团体名，路也是通的。上面这些邻居行就是它直接答的。": "This device accepts this community string and the path is fine. The neighbor rows above are its own direct answers.",
    "这台设备认这个团体名，路也是通的。下面 MAC 表、端口、PoE、LLDP 那几栏都可以问了。": "This device accepts that community string and the path is good. The MAC table, ports, PoE and LLDP columns below can all be asked now.",
    "这台读不到": "This unit can't be read",
    "这台问不出": "This Host Won't Answer",
    "这块口的 MTU": "MTU of this port",
    "这多半是一台非网管交换机或 hub —— 所以图上<b>没有</b>给它画节点：它没有能问出身份的东西。\n        要坐实就对那台上 SNMP 读 MAC 表，看这些地址是不是都从一个口学来的。": "This is most likely an unmanaged switch or a hub — so the map draws <b>no</b> node for it: it has nothing that would give up an identity.\n        To settle it, enter SNMP for that device and read its MAC table to see whether all these addresses were learned on one port.",
    "这就是「ping 得通一半」「插了 VPN 某个网段上不去」最常见的来源。": "This is the most common source of 'ping gets through halfway' and 'plug in VPN and one subnet won't come up'.",
    "这张表读到一半停住了（撞上限量，或者设备走着走着不往前走了）。": "This table stopped reading halfway (hit the limit, or the device stalled partway).",
    "这时候「能 ping 通」恰恰是假象，通的是自己。": "Here \"ping goes through\" is exactly the illusion - it's reaching itself.",
    "这是 /31 互联口：这一段的两个地址都能配给设备，没有「减掉网络地址和广播地址」这一步。": "This is a /31 interconnect link: both addresses of this span can be configured on a device, there's no 'minus the network and broadcast address' step.",
    "这是 NODATA：域名存在，只是没配你要的这类记录（比如只配了 A、没配 AAAA）。不是故障。": "This is NODATA: the domain exists, it just has no record of the type you asked for (e.g. only A, no AAAA). Not a fault.",
    "这是{0}，出处 {1} —— 协议规定的地址。{2}": "This is {0}, source {1} — an address defined by the protocol. {2}",
    "这是「有时候连得上有时候连不上」的根因：两条路由都能到一个地址，走哪条看内核当时怎么选。得改掩码或改地址池。": "This is the root cause of \"sometimes it connects, sometimes it doesn't\": two routes both reach one address, and which is taken depends on how the kernel picks at the moment. You need to change the mask or the address pool.",
    "这是「那台平台真把这台当设备」最硬的证据：它主动问了通道表，或者发了点播。": "This is the hardest evidence that \"the platform really treats this as a device\": it actively queried the channel table, or sent an on-demand request.",
    "这是一份主清单": "This is a master playlist",
    "这是一枚签名令牌，上面已经把头解出来 —— ★ 这里只解码，不验签，所以「解得开」不等于「这枚令牌有效」。载荷里常带账号、内部 IP，别整段贴进工单。": "This is a signed token; the header has been decoded above — ★ this only decodes, it doesn't verify the signature, so \"decodable\" doesn't mean \"this token is valid\". The payload often carries accounts and internal IPs; don't paste the whole thing into a ticket.",
    "这是编码端的 GOP / 切片间隔改了而平台没跟着改承诺值，两边对一遍。": "This is the encoder's GOP / slice interval changing while the streaming server didn't update its promised value; compare both sides.",
    "这是那一头的实现问题（或中间把这条头改掉了），不是口令错。": "This is the far end's implementation problem (or something in the middle rewrote this header), not a wrong password.",
